1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,816
Why do smart people stay in

2
00:00:01,816 --> 00:00:02,959
draining careers,

3
00:00:02,959 --> 00:00:04,506
dead-end side projects,

4
00:00:04,506 --> 00:00:07,061
and broken commitments for years after

5
00:00:07,061 --> 00:00:08,810
they clearly stop working?

6
00:00:08,810 --> 00:00:12,235
Behavioral scientists call it the Concorde Fallacy.

7
00:00:12,235 --> 00:00:14,854
Long before the supersonic Concorde jet

8
00:00:14,854 --> 00:00:15,996
launched in 1976,

9
00:00:15,996 --> 00:00:18,145
Britain and France knew it would

10
00:00:18,145 --> 00:00:19,086
lose fortunes.

11
00:00:19,086 --> 00:00:21,839
Yet both governments poured billions more

12
00:00:21,839 --> 00:00:23,854
in so prior spending would not

13
00:00:23,854 --> 00:00:24,660
look wasted.

14
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:26,953
Your brain hates admitting a loss

15
00:00:26,953 --> 00:00:29,454
so intensely that it throws precious

16
00:00:29,454 --> 00:00:32,511
future years after unrecoverable past years.

17
00:00:32,511 --> 00:00:34,457
Past time and past money are

18
00:00:34,457 --> 00:00:35,360
gone forever.

19
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:38,522
Break the spell with the Zero-Base Question:

20
00:00:38,522 --> 00:00:40,822
knowing everything I know today,

21
00:00:40,822 --> 00:00:42,835
if I were not already inside

22
00:00:42,835 --> 00:00:45,494
this project or commitment right now,

23
00:00:45,494 --> 00:00:47,650
would I enter it from scratch?

24
00:00:47,650 --> 00:00:49,944
If the honest answer is no,

25
00:00:49,944 --> 00:00:52,493
walking away is not quitting -

26
00:00:52,493 --> 00:00:55,296
it is freeing your future margin.

27
00:00:55,296 --> 00:00:56,146
Otherwise,

28
00:00:56,146 --> 00:00:57,420
ask yourself...
